  + [depends_on] is docs/surfaces/FSC4_Surface_Boundary_And_Invariant_Map.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/FSC4_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR5_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/P6_Surface_Projection_System_Final_Slices.v1.sop as the executable P6 final slice surface
  = must: execute P6-S01 before defining authority notices, surface envelopes, inbound action classification, projection fixtures, dependency posture, implementation activation, or downstream gates
  = must: execute P6-S02 before any surface-specific projection boundary consumes authority notice or freshness semantics
  = must: execute P6-S03 before inbound action classification consumes surface-specific boundary authority
  = must: execute P6-S04 before projection fixture snapshot planning becomes Spark-suitable
  = must: execute P6-S06 before adapter, UI, Langflow, IRC, Matrix, web, Codex, terminal, transport, or implementation activation work is reconsidered
  = must: keep UI implementation, adapter implementation, transport implementation, dependency installation, package metadata mutation, projection runtime execution, assignment, dispatch, operations control, and live machine control unauthorized
  - never: treat this canonical specification as permission to implement UI, adapters, transports, Langflow, IRC, Matrix, web, Codex, terminal integrations, assign work, dispatch work, control operations, or control the live machine

& [CanonicalP6FinalSliceSequence] is the accepted final slice sequence for P6
  + [slice] is P6-S01 boundary import and projection obligation inventory
  + [slice] is P6-S02 authority notice freshness and nonpromotion rendering contract
  + [slice] is P6-S03 multi-surface projection envelope and surface-specific boundary contract
  + [slice] is P6-S04 inbound action classification and surface mutation boundary contract
  + [slice] is P6-S05 projection fixture snapshot plan and generated projection nonpromotion boundary
  + [slice] is P6-S06 surface adapter Langflow dependency deferral and implementation activation boundary
  + [slice] is P6-S07 P6 completion review and downstream gate
  + [current_ready_slice] is P6-S01
  + [gated_slice] is P6-S02 until P6-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is P6-S03 until P6-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is P6-S04 until P6-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is P6-S05 until P6-S04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is P6-S06 until P6-S05 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is P6-S07 until P6-S06 accepted

  = must: preserve this order unless a completed-work review rebakes the P6 surface
  = must: mark downstream slices stale when upstream P6 output changes authority notice rendering, freshness display, nonpromotion display, surface envelope, inbound action classification, mutation boundary, fixture plan, dependency posture, implementation activation boundary, or downstream gate

& [CanonicalP6ModelRouting] is the model routing for P6 final slices
  + [P6-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [P6-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [P6-S03] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [P6-S04] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [P6-S05] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after P6-S04 acceptance unless projection authority, surface mutation, nonpromotion, or no-live-effect semantics change
  + [P6-S06] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [P6-S07] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: keep authority notice rendering, surface-specific boundaries, inbound action mutation, adapter posture, dependency posture, implementation activation, and downstream gates under deeper reasoning
  = must: treat bounded projection fixture snapshot planning as Spark-suitable only after authority display, surface envelope, and inbound action contracts are accepted and stable

